{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792954710,"nonce":"zn6kgKkPMDnikPXMxvwtaFObGL8=","title":"Deliver watched page completions before a host event wait","message":"RayDE's browser workspace session uses ash-channel futures. The full page mounts the remote directory and starts a supervised RayScript host, but a service call emitted after the first idle window frame remains undelivered until pointer or tab activity.\n\nThe future park loop polls registered page watches. host_wait did not, so a native event-loop wait could starve channel completions even when its bytes had arrived. Poll watches before advancing the scheduler, and expose the process-lifetime completion wake word so a browser window agent can wake its own event queue when it changes. Keep native event-loop deadline handling and wake registration intact.\n\nRelated RayDE track: ad5488521da444c1e399c16959e7312263ebadab165bcede9be64882738600c0. Full browser test reads a large remote file and answers an extension workspace call without pointer input. Runtime unit test checks host_wait delivers a changed watch before sleeping.","files":null}]}